# Git Blame Ignore Revisions
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# This file contains commit SHAs that should be ignored by git blame.
# Use this for mass formatting commits (Prettier, ESLint, etc.) that don't
# represent meaningful code changes.
#
# Usage:
#   1. Add commit SHAs to this file (one per line)
#   2. Git will automatically exclude these commits from blame output
#   3. Use 'git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs' to test
#
# To find formatting commit SHAs:
#   git log --oneline --grep="prettier\|eslint\|format" --all
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Example entries (replace with actual commit SHAs from your repos):

# Prettier migration - 2024-01-15
# a1b2c3d4e5f6789012345678901234567890abcd

# ESLint autofix - 2024-02-20
# f6e5d4c3b2a1098765432109876543210fedcba9

# Migrate to new code style - 2024-03-10
# 1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef12345678

# Automated whitespace cleanup - 2024-04-05
# abcdef1234567890abcdef1234567890abcdef12

# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# HOW TO ADD NEW ENTRIES:
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#
# 1. Find the commit SHA of the formatting change:
#    git log --oneline -n 20
#
# 2. Add the full 40-character SHA to this file with a descriptive comment
#
# 3. Commit this file to your repository:
#    git add .git-blame-ignore-revs
#    git commit -m "chore: ignore formatting commit in blame"
#
# 4. Verify it works:
#    git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs <file>
#
# ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
